            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SLJ6"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I loved this recipe!.....I used Fage Greek yogurt (non-fat), low fat sour cream......and made this sauce the day before I served it......The flavors and texture of the cucumber were excellent. I served this on Greek Style Garlic Chicken on this site in a whole wheat pita....hubster loved this sauce as well....Thanks 5THSISTER.....great recipe!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "joyello18"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wow this is sooo much better than any tzatziki I've had at the Greek/Mediterranean restaurants in my city. Used full fat greek yogurt instead of plain and did not strain it; lowfat regular sour cream. Used 1/2 of a large cucumber, did not skin or de-seed it. Threw all ingredients into the blender (since I don't like cucumber chunks). Used 1/2 tsp salt and 1/4 tsp pepper. It was very liquidy/runny, which was perfect as a topping for the spinach crepes I was making. Wow! Usually with ethnic foods I really have to mess with the balance of ingredients to be happy with it, but this one was perfect as written! Love it and so does the family.",
            "datePublished": "2010-07-17T18:10:10.583Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "AnnieDoodleAllTheDay"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used Greek yogurt for the additional tang, then added thinly sliced red onion for a pop of color for a party. Nice job putting this together - it's delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2021-05-27T18:38:25.447Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lorrie Klessig"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used Greek yogurt and let it drain for about an hour and also salted the cucumbers and let them sit on paper towels. The sauce was nice and thick. We used the extra sauce on salad the next day. Very good.",
            "datePublished": "2020-04-09T03:54:36.570Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tennismom"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was good but had to add a little more flavor as it was a little bland for our tastes. Added extra garlic, lemon juice, salt and pepper and 1/2 t dill, (the dill added a lot) also I halved the recipe it makes way too much for 4 people. Only used 1/2 the cucumber it was plenty...Finally I drizzled with olive oil to jazz up my fat free feta I had on hand. Didn't read to chill overnight but it was fine right away.",
            "datePublished": "2012-02-19T16:57:14.870Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tom"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I was guesstimating the measurements and may have used a tad too much feta. I omitted the oregano and used fresh dill &amp; mint. Used white pepper not black, didn't skin or seed the cucumbers, then threw it all in a blender. Last recipe I tried suggested cumin, coriander and oregano and that was awful. Liked this one much better",
            "datePublished": "2017-04-11T16:38:04.200Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tamie Jensen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The best I've ever made! I added 1/2 t. dried mint and 2 drops lemon essential oil because I had no lemon zest.",
            "datePublished": "2020-01-29T00:18:41.350Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Courtney Greenwood Steigerwald"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Not authentic,... an improvement over authentic imo. I have tried out different greek sauces and this is really fun with the feta in it. \nThings I did different because we like a bolder sauce: used greek yogurt instead of regular, two cloves of garlic, all the juice from a a small lemon, lots of chives from the garden instead of reg green onions. Also to make it less watery salting the cucumbers and draining and squeezing them to release as much water as possible.\n\nawesome...",
            "datePublished": "2011-09-20T08:36:15.043Z"
          },
          {
